## 17. Temporary files and harness state

Forbidden:

- `E:\GT-KB\.gtkb-state`
- `E:\GT-KB\harness-state`, absent an explicit one-time owner exception
- direct writes to generated harness projections

Canonical scratch root:

    E:\GT-KB\scratchpad

Use only the current session's subdirectory. Scratch is ephemeral and must not
survive the authoring session.

Canonical harness baseline:

    E:\GT-KB\.harness-baseline-configuration

`E:\GT-KB\memory` holds non-authoritative operational notes only. Nothing may
depend on it, and anything that must survive the session is written to the
database through a governed writer.

Until the Windows encoding defect is repaired, disclose and use
`PYTHONIOENCODING=utf-8` when required by affected Python tools.

