## 18. Orphan code

Reusable code must be integrated, usable, tested, and documented.

Do not retain stray code because it may be useful later. Code that is not wired
into GT-KB is dead and should be integrated through governed work or removed
through governed forward change.

Formal-closure notice: no active formal artifact governs orphan or unintegrated
code. Closure gap C-4.

## 19. Bridge filing during transition

All bridge artifacts must be:

1. filed through the governed CLI when that interface exists and accepts the
   filing; or
2. deposited as a complete validated top-level file in `E:\GT-KB\bridge` during
   the temporary transition.

When the governed CLI refuses a lawful filing, record the refusal evidence and
the substitution in the deposited artifact under section 15, and file the
correction under section 14.

Never access raw PostgreSQL coordination tables or hidden bridge storage.

